---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Article
  title={`Terms of Use — ${SITE.name}`}
  heading="Terms of use"
  kicker="Policy"
  description={`Terms of use for the ${SITE.name} website: what this site is, what it isn’t, and the basis on which its content is offered.`}
>
  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    This website describes the services of {SITE.name} and publishes general commentary on construction from
    the owner's perspective. Its content is offered in good faith and kept current with reasonable care.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Not legal advice.</strong> Nothing here is legal advice, and reading it creates no
      solicitor-client or attorney-client relationship. Construction agreements should be reviewed by a
      qualified construction lawyer in the project's jurisdiction.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Not an engagement.</strong> No content on this site, and no enquiry sent through it, creates a
      professional engagement. Engagements exist only under a written agreement signed by both parties, which
      alone defines the scope, fee, and terms of our work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Not construction services.</strong> {SITE.name} advises, reviews, verifies, coordinates, and
      reports on behalf of owners. We do not perform construction work, contract for it, or hire trades.
      Owners contract directly with their contractors.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    Construction outcomes depend on many parties and circumstances beyond any advisor's control. Nothing on
    this site promises a particular outcome, saving, schedule, or result — and you should be wary of any firm
    whose website does.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of content</h2>
  <p>
    Content is © {SITE.name}. You may quote it with attribution; you may not republish it wholesale or
    present it as your own. Trademarks and names of other organizations mentioned on this site belong to
    their owners.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    About these terms, or anything else: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="annotation not-prose mt-10">Last updated: August 2026.</p>
</Article>
